    "['set interfaces [interface_name]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.0\\n ipv6 enable\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. Juniper's `ge-1/0/0` interface naming translates to Huawei's `GigabitEthernet1/0/0` format\\n2. The subinterface `.0` is maintained in Huawei's syntax\\n3. `family inet6` in Juniper is equivalent to `ipv6 enable` in Huawei to enable IPv6 on the interface\\n4. The Huawei command must be entered in interface configuration mode (hence the `interface` prefix)\", 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ipv6 enable', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.0\\n ipv6 enable\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. Juniper's `ge-1/0/0` interface naming translates to Huawei's `GigabitEthernet1/0/0` format\\n2. The subinterface `.0` is maintained in Huawei's syntax\\n3. `family inet6` in Juniper is equivalent to `ipv6 enable` in Huawei to enable IPv6 on the interface\\n4. The Huawei command must be entered in interface configuration mode (hence the `interface` prefix)\", 'trans_template': 'ipv6 enable'}]]": 1,
