    "['set interfaces [interface]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/2', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/2\\n ipv6 enable\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The Juniper \"set interfaces ge-0/0/2 unit 0 family inet6\" command enables IPv6 on interface ge-0/0/2.0\\n2. The Huawei equivalent:\\n   - Uses \"GigabitEthernet\" instead of \"ge\" for interface naming\\n   - Doesn\\'t use subunit notation (\".0\") as Huawei handles this differently\\n   - Uses \"ipv6 enable\" to activate IPv6 on the interface\\n3. The Huawei command must first enter interface configuration mode before applying the IPv6 setting', 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/2'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ipv6 enable', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/2\\n ipv6 enable\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The Juniper \"set interfaces ge-0/0/2 unit 0 family inet6\" command enables IPv6 on interface ge-0/0/2.0\\n2. The Huawei equivalent:\\n   - Uses \"GigabitEthernet\" instead of \"ge\" for interface naming\\n   - Doesn\\'t use subunit notation (\".0\") as Huawei handles this differently\\n   - Uses \"ipv6 enable\" to activate IPv6 on the interface\\n3. The Huawei command must first enter interface configuration mode before applying the IPv6 setting', 'trans_template': 'ipv6 enable'}]]": 1,
